# A calculator. Nothing is stored: every capability takes numbers and gives one back.
#   ./intent build examples/calculator.intent -o build/calculator
#   echo "share 7,2" | build/calculator

Sum: take a number a and a number b and return a plus b.
Difference: take a and b and return a minus b.
Product: take two numbers a and b and return a times b.
Area: take a width and a height and return width times height.

# Dividing by zero has no answer, so the program has to say what it wants instead.
Share: take a and b and return a divided by b if b is not 0, otherwise 0.
Remainder: take a and b and return a modulo b if b is not 0, otherwise 0.

# A value can depend on a condition, and conditions can follow one another.
Bigger: take a and b and return a if a is over b, otherwise b.
Sign: take n and return 1 if n is over 0, otherwise -1 if n is under 0, otherwise 0.
Clamp: take n and return 0 if n is under 0, otherwise 100 if n is over 100, otherwise n.
Fee: take an amount and return amount times 2 divided by 100 if amount is over 1000, otherwise 20.
